// Shared test support for the TurboQuant KV writer (turbo2 / turbo3 / turbo4).
//   tests/test-turbo-write-host.cpp  CPU only: runs the SAME algorithm the CUDA kernels run (turbo-write.h) on the
//                                    host and compares it with quantize_row_turbo{2,3}_0_ref (ggml-turbo-quant.c).
//   tests/test-turbo-cpy.cpp         CUDA: GGML_OP_CPY / GGML_OP_SET_ROWS F32 -> turbo written by the GPU, compared
//                                    with the same host reference through the same verdict function.
// GENERATED by temp/_turbow_0929_gen_check_h.py: the sign tables below are read out of ggml-turbo-quant.c
// (turbo_cpu_s1 / turbo_cpu_s2), not retyped.
//
// THRESHOLDS ARE FIXED HERE, BEFORE ANY RUN (2026-09-29), and are not tuned afterwards:
//   kIdxMismatchMax  1e-3   fraction of the 128-element groups' centroid indices that differ from the reference.
//                           Expected exactly 0 on the host; the slack is for FMA contraction differences on the GPU.
//   kNormRelMax      1.5e-3 max relative difference of the fp16 block norm (one fp16 ulp is ~1e-3).
//   kNmseRefMax      1e-6   NMSE(dequant(candidate), dequant(reference)); both are in the rotated domain.
//   kReconNmseMax3   0.06   NMSE(un-rotated dequant(candidate), source). Lloyd-Max 3-bit on a Gaussian is ~0.035.
//   kReconNmseMax2   0.16   same for 2-bit (~0.118 for Lloyd-Max on a Gaussian).
// NEGATIVE CONTROL: the same writer with signs1 and signs2 swapped is a different rotation. That variant is run
// through this same verdict and MUST fail it (idx mismatch and NMSE far outside the limits); a verdict that passes
// it would not be measuring the rotation at all.

